The UK NCSC, with partner agencies, published [minimum forensic and logging features](https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/guidance/guidance-on-digital-forensics-protective-monitoring) buyers should demand from network device makers. A few that close these gaps:

- near-real-time remote logging over TLS, in a documented format;
- logs of logins, configuration changes, firmware updates and "attempts to clear, rotate, or manipulate log files";
- timestamps in UTC with milliseconds, and loud alerts when time sync fails;
- a heartbeat message that includes a "SHA256 digest of current configuration";
- a way to collect memory and full storage for investigation.

None of these is exotic on a server. On many appliances they are missing or off by default.

